1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,793
Every day, India's food brands write off stock that sells too slowly.

2
00:00:05,743 --> 00:00:09,525
Too close to its date for quick commerce, it's destroyed.

3
00:00:11,675 --> 00:00:15,049
Smart-Clearance turns that write-off into recovery.

4
00:00:15,049 --> 00:00:18,701
Agentic software as a service for FMCG.

5
00:00:19,101 --> 00:00:21,704
Under the hood, it's all Google Cloud.

6
00:00:22,204 --> 00:00:29,845
Four apps on Firebase, one API on Cloud Run, Cloud SQL as the record.

7
00:00:29,995 --> 00:00:35,111
Pub/Sub carries every step; Cloud Scheduler keeps the clock.

8
00:00:35,211 --> 00:00:41,337
Nine AI agents on Google's ADK read sales from BigQuery and photos from Cloud Storage.

9
00:00:41,637 --> 00:00:48,404
On Google's Agent Platform, Gemini Pro prices and negotiates, and Flash reads and writes.

10
00:00:48,454 --> 00:00:54,958
The models never touch the money: the API works out every figure, and a person says yes.

11
00:00:55,208 --> 00:01:07,653
Today, we're going to demo two journeys, live on production: Munchly Foods, an imaginary brand, with two batches at two distributors. One happy path, and one sad.

12
00:01:07,803 --> 00:01:14,179
Munchly, its distributors and kiranas share its workspace. Neha opens the console.

13
00:01:14,429 --> 00:01:23,194
In the console, Neha sets up a brand in minutes: its stock export, its people, its gates, its agents.

14
00:01:23,994 --> 00:01:29,174
The workspace installs as an app on any laptop, tablet or phone.

15
00:01:29,824 --> 00:01:34,014
Priya, who runs Munchly's supply chain, signs in.

16
00:01:35,114 --> 00:01:42,031
Her Command Center tracks every batch at risk: days left, sell-through, and the cost of the bin.

17
00:01:42,431 --> 00:01:50,094
From BigQuery's sell-through, the Watcher flags two batches: the Mango Drink and the Masala Chips.

18
00:01:50,894 --> 00:01:58,303
Lakshmi Agencies photographs the label, and Vision, on Gemini Flash, matches it to the stock export.

19
00:01:58,353 --> 00:02:10,111
From the batch's sales history and Munchly's own rules, the Valuer prices each exit and the Router splits it. Priya approves with one tap.

20
00:02:10,511 --> 00:02:19,543
Outreach offers the packs to fifty-eight kiranas in their own language; each order lands on Priya's screen, live.

21
00:02:19,793 --> 00:02:26,841
Fifty-two shops take thirteen hundred and seventy-two packets, each with its own GST invoice.

22
00:02:27,141 --> 00:02:34,517
The godown's staff buy a hundred and fifty packs by UPI, and Vision checks the receipt against the count.

23
00:02:34,567 --> 00:02:39,645
Feeding India collects the last fifty-eight packs, and issues a donation receipt.

24
00:02:40,195 --> 00:02:46,736
Paperwork files every paper in Cloud Storage, and Lakshmi Agencies ends whole.

25
00:02:48,386 --> 00:02:56,516
But not every batch sells. Munchly's Masala Chips go to Rakesh Traders' kiranas in Nagpur, and just two order.

26
00:02:56,566 --> 00:03:06,401
On ExpireSoon, an imaginary near-expiry marketplace, the Negotiator counters a bid, and seven hundred and seventy-two packs sell.

27
00:03:07,701 --> 00:03:11,778
Five hundred and forty packets are left when the window closes.

28
00:03:11,928 --> 00:03:18,153
On expiry day, Rakesh must destroy them through an authorised agency, and prove it.

29
00:03:18,203 --> 00:03:26,458
At the landfill he photographs it, and the officer, two witnesses and Rakesh sign the certificate.

30
00:03:26,708 --> 00:03:33,477
Vision checks the photos; only on Priya's second yes are the certificate and credit note issued.

31
00:03:34,527 --> 00:03:44,319
Every step is on the record: an append-only audit trail in Cloud SQL, and requests traced end to end in Cloud Trace, with OpenTelemetry.

32
00:03:44,469 --> 00:03:51,649
Even here, Munchly recovers eleven thousand seven hundred rupees, and Rakesh ends whole.

33
00:03:51,899 --> 00:03:57,761
Impact posts every batch to its ledger in BigQuery, ready for BRSR.

34
00:03:57,961 --> 00:03:59,482
Try the guided demo.
